@local = http://localhost:3030

### 1. REST Countries – manual HTTP request for Bulgaria:
#   GET /v2/name/Bulgaria HTTP/1.1
#   Host: restcountries.com
GET https://restcountries.com/v2/name/Bulgaria

### 1. Italy – only name, capital, region and population
GET https://restcountries.com/v2/name/Italy?fields=name,capital,region,population

### 1. German-speaking countries – only name and region
GET https://restcountries.com/v2/lang/de?fields=name,region

### 2. Bus Stop (valid ids: 1287, 1308, 1327, 2334)
GET {{local}}/jsonstore/bus/businfo/1287

### 3. Phonebook GET
GET {{local}}/jsonstore/phonebook

### 4. Phonebook POST
POST {{local}}/jsonstore/phonebook
Content-Type: application/json

{ "person": "Maya", "phone": "+1-555-7653" }

### 4. Phonebook POST (second entry)
POST {{local}}/jsonstore/phonebook
Content-Type: application/json

{ "person": "Peter", "phone": "+1-555-1234" }

### 5. Employees – all
GET https://dummy.restapiexample.com/api/v1/employees

### 5. Employees – one
GET https://dummy.restapiexample.com/api/v1/employee/1

### 5. Employees – create
POST https://dummy.restapiexample.com/api/v1/create
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "test", "salary": "123", "age": "23" }

### 5. Employees – update
PUT https://dummy.restapiexample.com/api/v1/update/21
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "test", "salary": "1123", "age": "23" }

### 5. Employees – delete
DELETE https://dummy.restapiexample.com/api/v1/delete/2

### 6. Firebase – create a book (set @firebase to your Realtime Database URL)
@firebase = https://your-project-default-rtdb.firebaseio.com
POST {{firebase}}/books.json
Content-Type: application/json

{ "genre": "Thrillers", "title": "Gone Girl", "author": "Gillian Flynn" }

### 6. Firebase – read all books
GET {{firebase}}/books.json

### 6. Firebase – delete a book (id returned by POST as "name")
DELETE {{firebase}}/books/{{bookId}}.json

### 7. Backendless – create a song
@backendless = https://api.backendless.com/{{appId}}/{{restApiKey}}
POST {{backendless}}/data/Music
Content-Type: application/json

{ "singer": "Alan Walker", "title": "Faded" }

### 7. Backendless – read all songs
GET {{backendless}}/data/Music

### 7. Backendless – delete a song
DELETE {{backendless}}/data/Music/{{objectId}}

### 8. Back4App – create a student
POST https://parseapi.back4app.com/classes/Students
X-Parse-Application-Id: {{appId}}
X-Parse-REST-API-Key: {{restApiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Sarah", "lastName": "Johnson", "averageGrade": 5.9 }

### 8. Back4App – read all students
GET https://parseapi.back4app.com/classes/Students
X-Parse-Application-Id: {{appId}}
X-Parse-REST-API-Key: {{restApiKey}}

### 8. Back4App – delete a student
DELETE https://parseapi.back4app.com/classes/Students/{{objectId}}
X-Parse-Application-Id: {{appId}}
X-Parse-REST-API-Key: {{restApiKey}}
